1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,640
The warnings came from me.

2
00:00:01,640 --> 00:00:02,160
I'm Mara.

3
00:00:02,160 --> 00:00:04,690
I can't speak, and I'm
running out of glass.

4
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:07,640
Now I'm the one
sending messages.

5
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:09,570
Inside nine, you can't speak.

6
00:00:09,570 --> 00:00:11,010
You can only bend glass.

7
00:00:11,010 --> 00:00:12,680
And the glass runs out.

8
00:00:12,990 --> 00:00:15,230
Through the wall, I
could see my shop.

9
00:00:15,230 --> 00:00:15,870
Last night.

10
00:00:15,870 --> 00:00:17,820
And me, not knowing a thing.

11
00:00:18,020 --> 00:00:18,710
I needed her.

12
00:00:18,710 --> 00:00:20,280
But I would have to ask.

13
00:00:20,480 --> 00:00:23,320
I have never asked anyone
for help in my life.

14
00:00:23,920 --> 00:00:25,230
So I wrote it.

15
00:00:26,530 --> 00:00:27,880
It says hello! It's friendly.

16
00:00:27,880 --> 00:00:28,640
I love it.

17
00:00:28,840 --> 00:00:31,500
I had forgotten how
much I love that idiot.

18
00:00:32,010 --> 00:00:33,060
I wrote tomorrow.

19
00:00:33,060 --> 00:00:33,860
I wrote nine.

20
00:00:33,860 --> 00:00:35,400
I wrote, don't turn.

21
00:00:35,790 --> 00:00:36,680
And she turned.

22
00:00:36,680 --> 00:00:37,930
Of course she turned.

23
00:00:37,930 --> 00:00:38,580
I did.

24
00:00:39,090 --> 00:00:41,570
Every one of you asks
yourself for help.

25
00:00:41,570 --> 00:00:43,910
And every one of
you comes alone.

26
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:46,900
Then a word lit up
that I did not write.

27
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:49,560
Here. In my mother's hand.

28
00:00:50,470 --> 00:00:52,260
And I had one tube left.
